    "turn_text": "Governor, I've talked to you about this before. I truly believe and I sincerely believe that you're making some of these decisions in what you believe to be the best interest of the people of the state of Ohio and around the country for that matter to prevent the spread of the disease and death. I don't question your motives at all. However, as we look at the 150 plus days since the shutdown began and we're seeing the economic impact and we know through CDC and World Health Organization numbers that for We're every job that's lost. I mean, we're looking at the rate of drug and alcohol abuse going up. We're looking at the rate of suicides going up. We're looking at the rate of depression cases going up. The longer the fear continues and the economic impact continues, we're creating more long-term problems. It seems like we should be looking for ways to facilitate more normalcy in the state rather than encouraging people to live in fear.",
